new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..965206bf5697
--- /dev/null
+++ b/llvm/docs/AMDGPUExternalAsmContract.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+AMDGPU external assembly call contract (experimental)
+====================================================
+
+This prototype provides a target-specific ABI for calls to external assembly
+leaf functions. It is intended for a fused AMDHSA kernel whose generated code
+must keep live values across an assembly operator. It uses ordinary LLVM calls
+with a versioned set of target attributes. SelectionDAG lowers the complete
+contract before register allocation; no MIR editing is involved.
+
+This is an experimental interface in this branch, not an upstream-supported
+ABI. An unmodified LLVM may ignore these string attributes. A producer must
+select a compatible toolchain and verify support, for example by checking that
+a call with an unsupported contract version is rejected.
+
+Version 1 scope
+---------------
+
+* AMDHSA, gfx1250, wave32, SelectionDAG (``-global-isel=0``).
+* A direct, non-tail call to an external declaration with ``ccc``. The
+  declaration must be ``convergent nounwind norecurse``.
+* The symbol denotes an assembly leaf function supplied at object-link time.
+  IR definitions, address escapes, aliases, signature casts, varargs and
+  implicit aggregate/stack arguments are rejected.
+* Arguments and results are 32/64-bit integers or 64-bit pointers. All argument
+  passing is explicit; the default device ABI's hidden workitem, workgroup,
+  kernarg and scratch arguments are not forwarded.
+* Return PC is in s[30:31]. The callee leaves s[30:39] unchanged, returns to that
+  PC, uses no private memory or LDS, makes no further calls, and does not end
+  the wave with ``s_endpgm``.
+* Entry and exit have full EXEC. All execution state, including MODE and VGPR
+  addressing MSBs, is preserved except declared SCC/VCC clobbers. Normal
+  gfx1250 call lowering resets addressing MSBs to zero before a call. A supplier
+  using high VGPR encodings must restore the MSBs before returning.
+* Dynamic VGPR allocation mode is not supported.
+* The supplier must complete pending memory/async operations before returning;
+  the normal AMDGPU call wait insertion handles caller operations at entry.
+  A memory-effect declaration alone is not a hardware fence or CTA barrier.
+
+Full EXEC is a caller precondition, not a consequence of ``convergent``. The
+caller must explicitly set ``"amdgpu-asm-full-wave-calls"="true"``. The backend
+also rejects calls under a statically identified divergent dominating branch
+that has not reconverged. This check is not a proof of arbitrary collective
+control flow: the producer remains responsible for the full-wave assertion,
+and for any required CTA-wide participation.
+
+Attributes
+----------
+
+``amdgpu-asm-contract``
+  Required version string, currently ``"1"``.
+
+``amdgpu-asm-arg-regs``
+  Required comma-separated input bindings in source argument order. Examples:
+  ``s0,s1,v[0:1],v2,v3,s2``. Empty for no parameters. A range is inclusive;
+  the lower-numbered register contains the low dword. A 64-bit pair must start
+  at an even register. Overlapping argument bindings are rejected.
+
+``amdgpu-asm-result-reg``
+  Required for non-void results, e.g. ``v4``, ``s4`` or ``v[8:9]``. A result
+  always clobbers its physical registers. It may reuse an input location.
+
+``amdgpu-asm-clobbers``
+  Required complete net-clobber list. Examples: ``s[4:7],v[4:15],v64,scc,vcc``.
+  Empty means no additional clobbers. All unlisted GPRs are preserved. The
+  backend clears every overlapping sub/superregister in its custom regmask.
+  The argument copies, call-target temporaries and return-PC definition remain
+  explicit machine operands, so their effects are included in liveness.
+
+``amdgpu-asm-vgpr-count`` / ``amdgpu-asm-sgpr-count``
+  Required decimal physical-register extents. They cover every input, output
+  and clobbered GPR and any internal temporary. SGPR extent is at least 32 to
+  cover the return-PC pair. These are numbered-register extents, not final HSA
+  metadata counts, and are merged into caller resource analysis. For example,
+  a callee using v95 requires a VGPR extent of at least 96 even if it uses only
+  a few individual registers.
+
+The declared extents are checked against the caller's target/workgroup and
+explicit allocation budget before register allocation. Their contribution to
+the final kernel resource count is merged during resource analysis. This
+prototype does not yet feed the callee's resource floor into every scheduler
+occupancy heuristic.
+
+``amdgpu-asm-private-bytes``
+  Required and must be ``"0"`` in version 1. This describes the assembly
+  supplier, not the compiler-generated caller's scratch requirements.
+
+Values passed to SGPRs must be known uniform by SelectionDAG's divergence
+analysis. Divergent values are rejected; the ABI does not implicitly discard
+other lanes through ``readfirstlane``. Fixed bindings do not guarantee absence
+of moves. Coalescing can eliminate a copy when source and destination already
+match, but otherwise normal register copies may be needed.
+
+Example
+-------
+
+.. code-block:: llvm
+
+  declare i32 @stage(i32, i32, i64, i32, i32, i32) #1
+
+  define amdgpu_kernel void @mono(ptr addrspace(1) %out) #0 {
+    %bx = call i32 @llvm.amdgcn.workgroup.id.x()
+    %by = call i32 @llvm.amdgcn.workgroup.id.y()
+    %tx = call i32 @llvm.amdgcn.workitem.id.x()
+    %ty = call i32 @llvm.amdgcn.workitem.id.y()
+    %address = ptrtoint ptr addrspace(1) %out to i64
+    %value = call i32 @stage(i32 %bx, i32 %by, i64 %address,
+                            i32 %tx, i32 %ty, i32 7)
+    ; The compiler can continue using caller values after the assembly call.
+    %slot = getelementptr i32, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %tx
+    store i32 %value, ptr addrspace(1) %slot
+    ret void
+  }
+
+  attributes #0 = { "amdgpu-asm-full-wave-calls"="true" }
+  attributes #1 = {
+    convergent nounwind norecurse
+    "amdgpu-asm-contract"="1"
+    "amdgpu-asm-arg-regs"="s0,s1,v[0:1],v2,v3,s2"
+    "amdgpu-asm-result-reg"="v4"
+    "amdgpu-asm-clobbers"="s[4:7],v[4:15],scc"
+    "amdgpu-asm-vgpr-count"="16"
+    "amdgpu-asm-sgpr-count"="32"
+    "amdgpu-asm-private-bytes"="0"
+  }
+
+The two s0/s1 values are separate u32 workgroup coordinates. The v0:v1 value is
+a 64-bit global address, not a four-dword buffer resource descriptor. Physical
+workgroup IDs, logical Mono task IDs and a supplier's tile coordinates remain
+the producer's responsibility.
+
+Spill policy and trust boundary
+------------------------------
+
+The call contract alone does not guarantee a spill-free caller. The independent
+``amdgpu-no-gpr-spill`` and ``amdgpu-no-private-memory`` policies enforce those
+requirements on generated code. Insufficient registers must produce an error,
+not an implicit scratch/LDS/global context-save fallback. A call mask protects
+live-through values; it is not a global cap on registers used by other stages.
+
+LLVM does not inspect an object which will only be supplied to a later linker.
+Its code-generation guarantees therefore assume the assembly declaration is
+truthful. A production integration needs an object/manifest identity check and
+binary audit at the packaging/link boundary. The accompanying ATOM prototype
+demonstrates that additional layer. A standalone launchable HSA code object is
+not automatically a callable function just because it is named ``.co``.
